// The data-level glow sample (glow v3, no mod DLL): a Rat that glows magenta from the moment it spawns.
// The status NAME is the request: FwGlow_<rrggbb> or FwGlow_<rrggbbaa> (hex, either case). mewframework recognises it
// in its apply_status hook and draws the rim through the combat outline mask with mods/fw-glow/shaders/fw_unit_glow.shader;
// the rim lasts as long as the unit carries the status (any vanilla removal ends it). Grant it through any mechanism
// that applies a status: StatusOnSpawnIn / StatusOnBattleStart on a character, an ability's effects, a Temporary.
// `spawn FwGlowRat` in a fight (or mods/fw-glow/tests/data-glow.mewtest). docs/data-mods.md "Asking for a unit glow from data".
FwGlowRat {
    variant_of Rat
    passives {
        StatusOnSpawnIn {
            FwGlow_ff00ff 1
        }
    }
}
